{"verdict":"approved","issues":[],"summary":"The diff is a minimal, correct fix that addresses the prescribed root cause exactly. Line 17 of apply-report-discounts.service.ts was changed from a direct string equality check (`lineItem.id === discount.lineItemId`) to using the existing `parseDispatchLineItemKey(lineItem.id).id` parser, which strips the '#return' suffix before comparison. This reuses the existing helper from src/services/helpers/order/dispatch-line-item-key.ts (re-exported via the helpers/order barrel) rather than hand-rolling string splitting. The import path (`../helpers/order`) correctly resolves through the barrel index. No `any` types are introduced; all function parameters and return types remain explicitly typed. Four vitest tests were added covering all three acceptance criteria: (1) return-trip discount line displays correct amount, (2) return-trip total selling price is reduced by the promo amount, (3) one-way trip still applies the discount correctly — plus a negative test for non-matching IDs. All 4 tests pass with exit code 0. No security concerns (no user-controlled paths, no API keys, no HTTP endpoints involved). No hardcoded strings — the '#' divider and 'return' tail are constants in the existing parser module. The change is 2 lines (1 import + 1 modified comparison), which is the most concise possible fix."}
